1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
This work is called SOAR-Flow — Safe Online Adaptive Refinement.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,800
Safe online fine-tuning: learn without danger, and need fewer safety corrections.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,600
The Flow policy proposes a driving reference.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
CBF–MPC certifies it and corrects risky references before execution.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,800
Protected returns are used for value calibration.

6
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:25,000
Paired corrections and future-intervention prediction guide the policy and gradually reduce auxiliary guidance.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Simulation uses SafeMetaDrive with new road layouts and obstacle configurations.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The initial policy-only execution fails in this new layout.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
With CBF–MPC enabled, the same policy is protected and passes safely.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,000
After online updates, the intermediate policy needs only occasional correction.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
At one million steps, the key segment is almost correction-free.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:02,000
With high-level correction disabled, the refined policy still completes the task.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Protected experience is converted into policy capability.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Return recovers while protected training cost and correction rate decrease.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
We next use a real uncrewed ground vehicle and collect left- and right-passing demonstrations.

16
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:39,000
We move the front obstacle to the right and block one demonstrated route.

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Early runs turn too late, so CBF–MPC corrects the reference. Later runs prepare earlier and need fewer corrections.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The eight-shaped task tests two successive turns in opposite directions.

19
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Early runs require correction; the intermediate behavior approaches the safe bypass pattern.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:19,000
The late policy completes the maneuver without high-level CBF correction, while low-level MPC tracking remains active.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:32,000
On the held-out cornering task, the frozen policy clears both obstacles without further updates.

22
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Compared with fixed CBF–MPC, it achieves higher success, shorter completion time, and larger minimum clearance.

23
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:54,000
SOAR-Flow combines safe interaction, calibrated values, and fewer corrections — a policy that keeps improving inside the safety boundary.
